The problem was inside calculating diff of city areas on viewport change and happened only with specific combination of previous/new city area lists. The error was swallowed by computation thread and wasn’t printed to logs, so the investigation took very long time.
Exception: 
{{java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: Comparison method violates its general contract!}}
{{at java.util.TimSort.mergeHi(TimSort.java:899)}}
{{at java.util.TimSort.mergeAt(TimSort.java:516)}}
{{at java.util.TimSort.mergeForceCollapse(TimSort.java:457)}}
{{at java.util.TimSort.sort(TimSort.java:254)}}
{{at java.util.Arrays.sort(Arrays.java:1492)}}
{{...}}

The exception is related to custom comparator which prioritises map update actions. Added potential fix, added tests for this comparator to avoid such issues in future, added logging of the exception for easier investigation in future.

