# *Section 8.3 (second one)*. After receiving a notice of default or criticism, the {color:#ff5630}Company{color} is to be afforded the opportunity to rectify the defects or deficiencies within a reasonable period of time by replacing the Temporary Worker about whom the notice of default has been made, before the Client submits a claim for damages or a price reduction. That which is deemed a reasonable period of time is to be determined with regard to the nature and extent of the defects or deficiencies and the possibility of providing replacement personnel.
# *Section 9.3*. Time for payment shall be of essence and failure to pay on time shall entitle the
Company to i) suspend the Assignment of the Temporary Worker, and ii)
immediately terminate the Agreement. {color:#ff5630}Bolt would like to have at least 14 days' notice in advance before the agreement is terminated due to delay in payment.{color}
# *Section 9.4*. Notwithstanding the Company's rights under Section 11.3 {color:#ff5630}below{color}, the Company
is entitled to compensation for payment reminders, debt recovery and costs
and interest according to the Statutory Interest Act.
# *Section 10.3(b)*. The Company may terminate this Agreement immediately by giving written
notice to the Client if it reasonably believes that any of the events described in clause {color:#ff5630}10.3 (a){color}
is likely to happen.
# *Section 10.6*. {color:#ff5630}Reference to section 8.4 is likely incorrect here, since it would make no sense. Which section was meant here?{color}
# *Section 13.1*. {color:#ff5630}Please delete this section. Company’s liability only in case of negligence in the selection process is unacceptable for Bolt.{color}
# {color:#ff5630}*Section 13.6*{color}{color:#ff5630}. The Client is not liable to the Company for any damages, unless the Client’s act or failure to act involves intentional misconduct, fraud, or a knowing violation of the law.{color}
# *Section 17*. Neither Party {color:#ff5630}may assign{color} any of its rights under this Agreement to a third party
without the prior written consent of the other Party.
