Hi [~accountid:602f9aeb871d30006843505c] 

Please see below the latest advice we have received  from the local lawyer in response to our questions about potential liability for errors and/or delays in communicating data.



_Regarding the private agreement between the VTC license holders and Bolt whereby Bolt assumes the obligation to communicate the data on their behalf, we would like to understand:_

_1.What kind of liability the VTC license holders may face with the Public Administration if they make mistakes or incur delays in communicating the data?_

 

{color:#ff5630}_Law 16/1987, dated 30 July, on the Ordination of Terrestrial Transports, in its most recent drafting in force since 2 October 2021, typifies in its article 140. 39.2 as a very serious breach the following infraction: "Commencement of a service without the holder of the authorisation (VTC) having communicated, by electronic means, the data relating to the service required by the legislation in force to the register of communications of vehicle hire services with driver of the Directorate General for Road Transport._{color}

 

{color:#ff5630}_The fine to be imposed for this infraction ranges from €1,001 up to €2,000. In those cases where the infraction is detected by the authorities, the vehicle shall be immobilised until the corresponding sanction is paid._{color}

{color:#ff5630} {color}

{color:#ff5630}_The imposition of three sanctions within a period of two years, by means of a final administrative decision, for the commission of this infringements, counted from the imposition of the first of them, in services carried out under the same VTC authorisation, may lead to the revocation of the VTC authorisation._{color}

{color:#ff5630} {color}

{color:#ff5630}_The applicable regulations don’t contemplate any specific sanction for those cases in which the data reported are wrong, It only contemplates as infraction the non-submission of the data before the commencement of the transport service._{color}

 

_2.Could we also face any liability vis-à-vis the Public Administration in our quality as ‘intermediary’ appointed by the VTC license holders if we transmit some erroneous data or make a late transmission?_

 

{color:#ff5630}_The responsible of this infringement before the Public Administration is the holder of the VTC license, as the one obliged by Law to submit the information_{color}_._

 

_3.What liability could we face if a VTC license holder comes after us in case of errors or delays in the transmission that we made on their behalf (and that has made them liable to the Public Administration)?_

{color:#ff5630}_The liability that you can face if a VTC license holder comes after you in case of delay that provoked the imposition of a fine, is the usual contractual liability. The VTC holder would be entitled to claim Bolt for the amount of the fine and for any additional damages suffered as a consequence of Bolt's actions. This liability can be limited in the T&Cs, however please note, as we indicated in our previous e-mail, that damages caused by wilful misconduct / gross negligence cannot be limited/excluded in case Spanish law is applicable-. In any event, the enforceability of the provisions may also depend on the manner they are accepted / capacity of negotiation of the counterpart, as the VTC license holders/fleet partners might construe that these are adhesion contracts._{color}

