Steps for achieving the migration:

1 - Update all existing endpoints and stop storing/getting data from {{profile.template_name}} and {{profile.name}} 
 1.1 - We would need an alter to make name nullable, but since we are deleting it we can just add a placeholder on the code
2 - Update the profile table with the following commands (double check the need of length 255 for all fields):

{code:sql}alter table profile
	add email varchar(255) null;

alter table profile
	add payment_method_type varchar(255) null;

alter table profile
	add payment_method_id varchar(255) null;

alter table profile
	add company_name varchar(255) null;

alter table profile
	add company_address varchar(255) null;

alter table profile
	add company_vat_code varchar(255) null;

alter table profile
	add company_registration_code varchar(255) null;{code}

3 - Start populating the new profile columns in the existing add/update endpoints (still keep populating the “profile_fields)
  3.1 - We must use a IFNULL command on the query that gets the profile data, so the next fields get priority to be displayed

{noformat}select IF_NULL(p.email, pf.email), ... from profile p inner join profile_field pf ...

// this will require subqueries once we need to transverse the fields table to get pf.email
// query can be slow we must ensure we have the correct index.{noformat}


4 - Copy the data from the existing data from the {{profile_fields}} to the new columns in the profile table
  4.1 - This can be done in a cron or a procedure, we just need to make sure to get the profile_field that is most recent:

{noformat}select ... from profile_field where profile_id = ${id} order by created desc limit 1;

// code for transversing the fields into columns is done at BillingProfileTable{noformat}

5 - Stop writing/deleting data to/from the {{profile_fields}} table. 
6 - Delete the table {{profile_fields}} and the columns {{profile.template_name}} and {{profile.name}}
 6.1 - Update the query to remove the “if_null” fallback
7- Last but not least we can adjust the size of the new columns of the profile table, and make email not-null

