Hi\!

The legal team is not able to pull out data on our users, including the IP address. This can be asked from the technical support. 

The privacy team is not opposing giving data out to police but certain requirements should be met in order for these requests to be valid and purposeful. Often we receive requests where the data requested is not specified, nor is the purpose what is it needed for. We, as the controller of data, need to make sure that the data given out is necessary for the purpose and also to follow the data minimisation principle. So, if the police request is too vague (eg. asking for all data about a user in bulk, not specifying the user or any identifying details etc), then we need to ask the police, if possible, to limit the scope and bring out the purpose why they need the data. I would think that the local criminal laws would also foresee the necessity for that.

Second, as a matter of general rule we allow our local subsidiaries/partner markets to respond to police requests directly when request for disclosure of personal data meets all the following conditions:

(a) the Personal Data is requested in connection with alleged crime;

(b) the request is presented on the law enforcement agency's letterhead;

(c) the request is duly signed and stamped by the appropriate law enforcement officer who is empowered by local law to represent the law enforcement agency that is making the request, and the Contractor has taken reasonable steps to validate the identity and authority of the officer;

(d) the request includes all the following elements: 

(i) all known email addresses, names, and phone numbers of the User(s) whose Personal Data is requested or description of the time, date, card details and other information which allows us to reasonably identify the user;

(ii) precise description of information requested, reasoning of why information is requested, and how it pertains to investigation of the alleged crime;

(iii) reference to applicable provisions of the relevant law under which the agency is entitled to request the information.

So if the request is deemed valid and purposeful and necessary by the local team, then you may proceed with providing the data.
